 "notes": "Columns on this leaf: 2-4 Population (whole state, recorded as area 'Hyderabad State'), 5-7 Hyderabad City, 8-10 Atraf-i-Balda, 11-13 Warangal; table continues on leaves 231-233 (other districts). Hierarchy as printed: 'Intermediate group' (Gondi) is included in the Dravidian Family total under (a) Vernaculars of the State (State: 6,972,534 + 1,652,068 + 76,087 = 8,700,689; Warangal likewise), so its lang_path is [A, (a), Dravidian Family]. Print inconsistencies (figures kept as printed, re-read at high zoom): (1) Hyderabad State, (b) Indo-European Family persons printed 161,081 but M+F = 161,084 and the Indo-Aryan Branch row prints 161,084 (and (b) 190,134 = 29,050 + 161,084). (2) Hyderabad State, Panjabi persons printed 1,560 but M+F = 3,630 + 930 = 4,560; Indo-Aryan Branch 161,084 also requires 4,560. (3) 'A' Vernaculars of India persons and males exceed (a)+(b)+(c) by 3 in both Hyderabad State (14,418,595 / 7,357,576 vs 14,418,592 / 7,357,573) and Hyderabad City (455,035 / 239,293 vs 455,032 / 239,290); consequently TOTAL persons/males are 3 less than A+B+C in both columns (State 14,436,148 vs 14,436,151; City 466,894 vs 466,897). P=M+F holds for the printed A rows. A stray '1' mark appears in the gutter to the left of the first three rows of the Population column; not a figure, ignored."
